d> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8021169-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8021169</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="WO-1993025792-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1993025792</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1094342A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OYAMA NOBUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>S T I JAPAN KK</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KABUSHIKI KAISHA S.T.I. JAPAN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OYAMA, NOBUO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OYAMA NOBUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OYAMA, NOBUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A luminous intensity distribution control device and a luminous flux density control device capable of applying sufficient rays of light to shadowed or poorly illuminated regions or portions because of structures and other objects by means of luminous intensity distribution control or luminous flux density control including light diffusion, refraction and splitting, wherein sunbeams are diffused by transparent bodies installed above two buildings and allowed to reach regions or portions that have conventionally been shadowed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un dispositif de commande de la répartition d'intensité lumineuse ainsi qu'un dispositif de commande de la densité du flux lumineux. Ces dispositifs permettent d'envoyer suffisamment de rayons lumineux vers des zones ou des parties qui sont situées dans l'ombre ou qui sont mal éclairées à cause de structures ou d'autres objets. Ces dispositifs vont réguler la répartition de l'intensité lumineuse ou la densité du flux lumineux, y compris en ce qui concerne la diffusion, la réfraction et la séparation de la lumière. Les rayons du soleil sont diffusés par des corps transparents installés au-dessus de deux bâtiments, et vont ainsi atteindre les régions ou les parties qui se trouvait alors dans l'ombre.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>